StringData.data:
An AI chip installed on the cerebrum of VEP-01 “Destroyer."
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Caligo Mainframe{color:end}

The blueprints for the Pulverizer.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Caligo Munitions Factory{color:end}

Blueprints for a prototype GT-99.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}
Can be found: Caligo Arms Facility{color:end}

The internal security console for GT-9A.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Caligo Tesla Lab{color:end}

A Shadow Hunter's eye. Said to be able to see through darkness.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Rentu Research Wing{color:end}

The outer panel from a waste incinerator. Made out of extremely solid material.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Rentu Disposal Center{color:end}

The Super Cannon for DH-07.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Rentu Trial Facility{color:end}

The completed mechanical heart of a drone.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Rentu Breeding Chamber{color:end}

The thick and sturdy tendon of Gigantos.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Lacrimosa Derelict{color:end}

The C-428 Reaper's Wings detached from Atlas's weapon. Very light for its size.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Highcrest Industrial Tower{color:end}

A sturdy tooth of the Monarch Worm that can even drill through diamonds.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Lacrimosa Station{color:end}

Koros's Jawbone. Seems to be magnetic.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Lacrimosa Power Plant{color:end}

The ritual mask for High Priest Mosra.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Karith Forest{color:end}

The greatsword of the traitor Usak.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Karith Tribal Grounds{color:end}

A crystal ball used by Vimumu. It is said to blessed by Atlas.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Drops in: Karith Sanctuary{color:end}

A headpiece belongings to the powerful necromancer A'ula. It is in the shape of an owl.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Drops in: Karith Caverns{color:end}

Za'bulu's Tail. It has become metallic after being infused with nanomachines.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Nuuran Outskirts{color:end}

A part of the Environment Converter that once turned Nuuran into a desert.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Nuuran Ghost Town{color:end}

The carapace of an aggressive desert spider.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Nuuran Battlefield{color:end}

The eye of a dead chimera. You feel as if it can see into your soul when you look at it.
Used as augmentation material stage 3.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Nuuran Ruins{color:end}

An insignia that the Blackram carry around.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Black Ram Supply Chain
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

A talisman that the Blackram carry around.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Black Ram Supply Chain
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

A home for languid spirits. Some glowing green stones are stuck on it.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Fire Temple
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

The remains of flame spirits. You can still feel the heat.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Fire Temple
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

The tattered armor of a fallen knight.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Gludio Dungeon
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

Paper with illegible writing. Looks like an official order.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: - Gludio Dungeon
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

The large mandible of an ant. Stronger than you would have expected from an insect's tooth.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Ant Nest
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

The wing of a large ant. Stronger than you would think.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Ant Nest
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

A teardrop crystal with an ominous aura.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Ascalonian Catacombs
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

A rune with dark aura.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Ascalonian Catacombs
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

A badge given to heroes who stop the privy council.

{color:#edec72}Can be found: Timespace Distortion - Independence Port
The Timespace Distortion can only be entered at specific times.{color:end}

